### =============================================================
### OWASP A09 – Security Logging and Monitoring Failures
### =============================================================
### Two problems:
###   (a) The password is logged in cleartext on registration
###   (b) Card data is logged on payment
###
### How to see it?
###   Watch the console of the running app – the sensitive data shows up
###   in the log output.
###   In production these logs flow into Splunk, ELK, Loki – readable by
###   ops teams, CI systems, external contractors.
### =============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5218

# ⚠️ Paste alice's token from 00_setup.http (needed for the payment log):
@aliceToken = PASTE_ALICE_TOKEN_HERE


### --- (a) Password in the log: registration ---
# After this request, look at the API terminal:
#   info: New user registered: Username=logvictim, Password=meinGeheimesPasswort123!, Email=...
#
# The log entry contains the password in CLEARTEXT – not even hashed.
# Why it's serious: logs are often kept for 30–365 days and streamed to
# monitoring systems with broad access.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "logvictim",
  "email": "logvictim@example.com",
  "password": "meinGeheimesPasswort123!"
}

###

### --- (b) Card data in the log: payment ---
# First create an order – the next request picks up its id automatically.
# @name logOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": 5, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

###

### --- (b) Pay – and watch the log ---
# After this request, look at the API terminal:
#   info: Payment processed: OrderId=X, Card=4111111111111111, CVV=999, Holder=Max Mustermann
#
# PCI-DSS explicitly forbids storing the CVV – logs included.
# Card numbers may only be stored masked (e.g. ****1111).
# The orderId comes from the previous request automatically (@name logOrder).
POST {{baseUrl}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{logOrder.response.body.$.id}},
  "cardNumber": "4111111111111111",
  "cardHolder": "Max Mustermann",
  "cvv": "999",
  "expiryDate": "06/28"
}
